/-!
# Discharging the per-package completion of the open/closed glue

Sources: Lank--Pauwels, *Gluing weak approximability along recollements* (LP26),
Lemma 4.3 (`lem:normalize`), Setup 4.4 (`setup:standing`) and Theorem 1.1;
A. Neeman, *Bounded t-structures on the category of perfect complexes*,
Acta Math. 233 (2024), Definition 2.9, Corollary 2.8 and Theorem 3.2(iii)--(iv);
Stacks Project Tag 09SR.

`Scheme/OpenClosedGlue.lean` reduced the open/closed step of the qcqs induction
for `NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability` to `NeemanCompactOpenClosedCompletionInput`
(deleted in wave 6 as superseded by this file):
for **every** pair of standard endpoint approximation packages `WZ`, `WU` it asks
for a recollement seed `I` together with

* isomorphisms `WZ.G ≅ i^*(G'[m] ⊕ j_!G_U)` and `WU.G ≅ G_U`, and
* bounded equivalences between the standard and the seed `t`-structures,

plus coproducts and `CompactHomZeroAtTop`.  The isomorphism fields tie the
geometry to the arbitrary generator the endpoint package happens to carry.

This module removes that dependence.

## What is proved

* `exists_changeGenerator` (no inputs): weak
  approximation data with generator `G` give weak approximation data, with the
  **same** `t`-structure, for any compact zero-detecting `H` such that `G` and `H`
  lie in each other's finite thick envelopes.  This is the generator-independence
  of weak approximability (Neeman, Remark 2.11 / LP26 §2.1.2) in the paper's
  coproduct-envelope form.  The ingredients, proved here, are: the finite thick
  envelope of `H` lies in `⋃ₙ ⟨H⟩^[-n,n]`; `⟨G⟩^[a,b] ⊆ ⟨H⟩^[a-n,b+n]` when
  `G ∈ ⟨H⟩^[-n,n]`; and eventual Hom vanishing into `t^{≤ -N}` propagates along
  the thick envelope.
* `tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass`: with Stacks 09SR, a `t`-structure
  in Neeman's preferred class is boundedly equivalent to the `t`-structure
  compactly generated by **any** compact zero-detecting generator (Neeman,
  Corollary 2.8, via the proved `tStructureEquivalent_of_isClassicalGeneratorOnCompacts`).
* `OpenClosedFrame`: the LP26 Lemma 4.3 / Setup 4.4 data of an open/closed
  recollement **without** any approximation package (it is
  `PaperOpenEndpointSetup` with the field `approxU` replaced by compactness and
  zero detection of `G_U`).  `satisfiesPaperWAAt_of_frame` then glues
  approximation data at *any* endpoint generators and any `t`-structures in the
  preferred class, and returns data at any middle `t`-structure in the preferred
  class.
* `OpenClosedFrameInput` (a frame for each qcqs open/closed situation) and
  `SupportedCategoryInput` (per-category facts) give the compact open/closed
  field (`compact_open_closed_glue_of_frameInput`) and the headline
  `neemanSupported_of_qcqs_of_frameInput`.

## What is assumed (all explicit hypotheses, none hidden)

* `Tag09SRPaper` -- Stacks Tag 09SR, direction (2) ⇒ (1), single generator:
  in a triangulated category with coproducts, a compact zero-detecting object
  classically generates the compact objects.  AxiomMath/Stacks:
  `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_iff_triangEnvelope_eq_isCompactObject_and_isCompactlyGenerated`
  (`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Triangulated/CompactObjects/CompactGenerators.lean`),
  with `IsCompactObject.{v}` rendered as `RelativeWeakApprox.IsCompactAb` and
  `IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator (singleton E)` as `IsPaperGenerator E`
  (both are "Hom from all shifts vanishes ⇒ zero").  It is taken as a named
  hypothesis because `StacksInput.lean` is a shared file; see
  `results/ASSUMPTIONS.md`.
* `neeman_3_2_iii` field of `SupportedCategoryInput` -- Neeman 2024,
  Theorem 3.2(iii): the restricted standard `t`-structure on `D_qc,Z(X)` is in
  the preferred equivalence class.  Not a Stacks result and not the allowed
  direction of Theorem 3.2, hence a named hypothesis.
* `HasCoproducts` and `CompactHomZeroAtTop` of the `D_qc,Z(X)` model -- the
  same two fields the existing completion already carried.
* `OpenClosedFrameInput` -- the recollement of `D_qc,Z∖V(X)`, `D_qc,Z(X)`,
  `D_qc,Z∩V(V)` with LP26 Lemma 4.3 normalization data and three compactly
  generated `t`-structures (GL26 Appendix A; Alonso--Jeremías--Souto).  Unlike
  the completion it does not depend on any approximation package.  It is no
  stronger than the existing seed: `OpenClosedFrame.ofPaperOpenEndpointSetup`
  forgets the seed's open package.  No concrete frame for the `D_qc` model is
  constructed in the tree (nor was a concrete seed).
* the affine supported base `of_isAffine` and Stacks 08DF
  (`StacksSupportedExcisionInput`), unchanged from the existing assembly;
  isomorphism transport is proved.

## Deviations

None of the paper statements is reworded.  The headline is the existing qcqs
statement of `NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability` (Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2(iv))
with the open/closed field supplied by the inputs above instead of the
per-package completion.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace RelativeFM.OpenClosedCompletionW3

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated CategoryTheory.Triangulated
open RelativeFM RelativeWeakApprox RelativeWeakApprox.PaperM2
open RelativeFM.NeemanPreferredM6
open ZeroObject

universe v u uZ uD uU

section Abstract

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C]
  [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ]
  [∀ (n : ℤ), (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]

/-! ### The bounded coproduct envelope `⋃ₙ ⟨H⟩^[-n,n]` -/

/-- Objects lying in some symmetric coproduct envelope `⟨H⟩^[-n,n]`. -/
def BoundedEnvelope (H : C) : ObjectProperty C := fun X =>
  ∃ n : ℤ, 0 ≤ n ∧ envelope H (-n) n X

lemma self_mem_envelope_zero (H : C) : envelope H 0 0 H :=
  lemma_3_1_1_contains H 0 0 H
    ⟨0, le_rfl, le_rfl, ⟨by simpa using (shiftFunctorZero C ℤ).symm.app H⟩⟩

lemma zero_mem_envelope_zero (H : C) : envelope H 0 0 (0 : C) := by
  refine ⟨H⟦-(0 : ℤ)⟧,
    Coprod.of_mem _ ⟨0, le_rfl, le_rfl, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩, ⟨?_⟩⟩
  exact ⟨0, 0, (isZero_zero C).eq_of_src _ _⟩

instance (H : C) : (BoundedEnvelope H).ContainsZero :=
  ⟨⟨0, isZero_zero C, 0, le_rfl, zero_mem_envelope_zero H⟩⟩

instance (H : C) : (BoundedEnvelope H).IsStableUnderShift ℤ where
  isStableUnderShiftBy a := ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderShiftBy.mk <| by
    intro X hX
    obtain ⟨n, hn, hX⟩ := hX
    rw [ObjectProperty.prop_shift_iff]
    refine ⟨n + |a|, by positivity, ?_⟩
    have h := map_shift_envelope H (-n) n a hX
    exact lemma31_2_mono H (by have := le_abs_self a; omega)
      (by have := neg_abs_le a; omega) _ h

instance (H : C) : (BoundedEnvelope H).IsStableUnderRetracts where
  of_retract := by
    intro X Y r hY
    obtain ⟨n, hn, hY⟩ := hY
    have := lemma_3_1_1_summands H (-n) n
    exact ⟨n, hn, ObjectProperty.prop_of_retract _ r hY⟩

instance (H : C) : (BoundedEnvelope H).IsTriangulatedClosed₂ := by
  apply ObjectProperty.IsTriangulatedClosed₂.mk'
  intro T hT h₁ h₃
  obtain ⟨n₁, hn₁, h₁⟩ := h₁
  obtain ⟨n₃, hn₃, h₃⟩ := h₃
  let n := max n₁ n₃
  have := lemma_3_1_1_extensions H (-n) n
  refine ⟨n, le_trans hn₁ (le_max_left _ _), ?_⟩
  exact ObjectProperty.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₂ _ T hT
    (lemma31_2_mono H (by have := le_max_left n₁ n₃; omega) (le_max_left _ _) _ h₁)
    (lemma31_2_mono H (by have := le_max_right n₁ n₃; omega) (le_max_right _ _) _ h₃)

instance (H : C) : (BoundedEnvelope H).IsTriangulated where

/-- The finite thick envelope of `H` lies in a bounded coproduct envelope. -/
theorem triangEnvelope_le_boundedEnvelope (H : C) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton H).triangEnvelope ≤ BoundedEnvelope H := by
  rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope_le_iff, ObjectProperty.singleton_le_iff]
  exact ⟨0, le_rfl, by simpa using self_mem_envelope_zero H⟩

/-- If `G ∈ ⟨H⟩^[-n,n]`, then `⟨G⟩^[a,b] ⊆ ⟨H⟩^[a-n,b+n]`.  This is the
minimality of LP26 Lemma 3.1(1) together with the shift formula 3.1(2). -/
theorem envelope_le_envelope_of_mem [HasCoproducts.{v} C] {G H : C} {n : ℤ}
    (hG : envelope H (-n) n G) (a b : ℤ) :
    envelope G a b ≤ envelope H (a - n) (b + n) := by
  have : ∀ J : Type v, (envelope H (a - n) (b + n)).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape
      (Discrete J) := fun J => lemma_3_1_1_coproducts H (a - n) (b + n) J
  have := lemma_3_1_1_extensions H (a - n) (b + n)
  have := lemma_3_1_1_summands H (a - n) (b + n)
  apply lemma_3_1_1_minimal
  rintro X ⟨k, hak, hkb, ⟨e⟩⟩
  have h := map_shift_envelope H (-n) n (-k) hG
  exact (envelope H (a - n) (b + n)).prop_of_iso e.symm
    (lemma31_2_mono H (by omega) (by omega) _ h)

/-! ### Eventual Hom vanishing into a `t`-structure -/

/-- Objects all of whose maps into `t^{≤ -N}` vanish, for some `N`. -/
def HomVanishesBelow (t : TStructure C) : ObjectProperty C := fun X =>
  ∃ N : ℤ, ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄, t.le (-N) Y → ∀ f : X ⟶ Y, f = 0

instance (t : TStructure C) : (HomVanishesBelow t).ContainsZero :=
  ⟨⟨0, isZero_zero C, 0, fun _ _ _ => (isZero_zero C).eq_of_src _ _⟩⟩

instance (t : TStructure C) : (HomVanishesBelow t).IsStableUnderShift ℤ where
  isStableUnderShiftBy a := ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderShiftBy.mk <| by
    intro X hX
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hX
    rw [ObjectProperty.prop_shift_iff]
    refine ⟨N + |a|, fun Y hY f => ?_⟩
    have hY' : t.le (-N) (Y⟦-a⟧) := by
      have h := t.le_shift (-(N + |a|)) (-a) (-(N + |a|) + a) (by ring) Y hY
      exact t.le_monotone (by have := le_abs_self a; omega) _ h
    have h0 := hN hY' ((shiftShiftNeg X a).inv ≫ f⟦-a⟧')
    have h1 : f⟦-a⟧' = 0 := by
      rw [← cancel_epi (shiftShiftNeg X a).inv, comp_zero]
      exact h0
    apply (shiftFunctor C (-a)).map_injective
    rw [h1, Functor.map_zero]

instance (t : TStructure C) : (HomVanishesBelow t).IsStableUnderRetracts where
  of_retract := by
    intro X Y r hY
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hY
    refine ⟨N, fun Z hZ f => ?_⟩
    calc f = (r.i ≫ r.r) ≫ f := by rw [r.retract, Category.id_comp]
      _ = r.i ≫ (r.r ≫ f) := Category.assoc _ _ _
      _ = 0 := by rw [hN hZ (r.r ≫ f), comp_zero]

instance (t : TStructure C) : (HomVanishesBelow t).IsTriangulatedClosed₂ := by
  apply ObjectProperty.IsTriangulatedClosed₂.mk'
  intro T hT h₁ h₃
  obtain ⟨N₁, hN₁⟩ := h₁
  obtain ⟨N₃, hN₃⟩ := h₃
  refine ⟨max N₁ N₃, fun Y hY f => ?_⟩
  have hY₁ : t.le (-N₁) Y := t.le_monotone (by have := le_max_left N₁ N₃; omega) _ hY
  have hY₃ : t.le (-N₃) Y := t.le_monotone (by have := le_max_right N₁ N₃; omega) _ hY
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Triangle.yoneda_exact₂ T hT f (hN₁ hY₁ _)
  rw [hg, hN₃ hY₃ g, comp_zero]

instance (t : TStructure C) : (HomVanishesBelow t).IsTriangulated where

/-- Eventual vanishing into `t^{≤ -N}` propagates along a finite thick
envelope. -/
theorem triangEnvelope_le_homVanishesBelow (t : TStructure C) {G : C}
    (hG : HomVanishesBelow t G) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelope ≤ HomVanishesBelow t := by
  rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope_le_iff, ObjectProperty.singleton_le_iff]
  exact hG

/-! ### Change of generator -/

/-- **Generator independence of weak approximability.**  Weak approximation
data `W` with generator `G` produce weak approximation data with the same
`t`-structure and generator any compact zero-detecting `H` for which `G` and
`H` lie in each other's finite thick envelopes.  No input is used. -/
theorem exists_changeGenerator
    [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated C] [HasCoproducts.{v} C]
    (W : PaperWeakApproximationData C) {H : C}
    (hHc : IsCompactAb H) (hHg : IsPaperGenerator H)
    (hGH : (ObjectProperty.singleton H).triangEnvelope W.G)
    (hHG : (ObjectProperty.singleton W.G).triangEnvelope H) :
    ∃ W' : PaperWeakApproximationData C, W'.G = H ∧ W'.t = W.t := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn, hGn⟩ := triangEnvelope_le_boundedEnvelope H W.G hGH
  have hGminus : W.t.minus W.G := ⟨W.A, ⟨W.G_mem_le⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (((ObjectProperty.singleton W.G).triangEnvelope_le_iff
    (Q := W.t.minus)).mpr (ObjectProperty.singleton_le_iff.mpr hGminus)) H hHG
  have hGvan : HomVanishesBelow W.t W.G := ⟨W.A, fun _ hY f => W.hom_vanishing hY f⟩
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := triangEnvelope_le_homVanishesBelow W.t hGvan H hHG
  let A' : ℤ := max (max (W.A + n) a) (max N 1)
  have hA₁ : W.A + n ≤ A' := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_left _ _)
  have hA₂ : a ≤ A' := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) (le_max_left _ _)
  have hA₃ : N ≤ A' := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_right _ _)
  have hA₄ : 1 ≤ A' := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) (le_max_right _ _)
  refine ⟨
    { G := H
      t := W.t
      A := A'
      A_pos := by omega
      G_compact := hHc
      G_paperGenerates := hHg
      G_mem_le := W.t.le_monotone hA₂ _ ha.le
      hom_vanishing := fun {Y} hY f => hN (W.t.le_monotone (by omega) Y hY) f
      exists_triangle := by
        intro F hF
        obtain ⟨E, D, f, g, h, hT, hE, hD⟩ := W.exists_triangle F hF
        refine ⟨E, D, f, g, h, hT, ?_, hD⟩
        have hE' := envelope_le_envelope_of_mem hGn (-W.A) W.A E hE
        exact lemma31_2_mono H (by omega) (by omega) E hE' }, rfl, rfl⟩

/-! ### Stacks 09SR and Neeman's preferred class -/

/-- **Stacks Tag 09SR**, direction (2) ⇒ (1), for a single generator: in a
triangulated category with small coproducts, a compact object detecting zero by
its shifts classically generates the compact objects.

AxiomMath/Stacks:
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_iff_triangEnvelope_eq_isCompactObject_and_isCompactlyGenerated`,
with `IsCompactObject.{v}` rendered by `IsCompactAb` and
`(ObjectProperty.singleton E).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` by `IsPaperGenerator E`.
The coproduct hypothesis of the tag is the antecedent. -/
def Tag09SRPaper (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C]
    [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ]
    [∀ (n : ℤ), (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C] : Prop :=
  HasCoproducts.{v} C →
    ∀ G : C, IsCompactAb G → IsPaperGenerator G → IsClassicalGeneratorOnCompacts G

/-- Generator change with the thick-generation hypotheses supplied by
Stacks 09SR. -/
theorem exists_changeGenerator_of_tag09SR
    [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated C] [HasCoproducts.{v} C] (h09 : Tag09SRPaper C)
    (W : PaperWeakApproximationData C) {H : C}
    (hHc : IsCompactAb H) (hHg : IsPaperGenerator H) :
    ∃ W' : PaperWeakApproximationData C, W'.G = H ∧ W'.t = W.t :=
  exists_changeGenerator W hHc hHg
    (h09 inferInstance H hHc hHg W.G W.G_compact)
    (h09 inferInstance W.G W.G_compact W.G_paperGenerates H hHc)

/-- **Neeman, Corollary 2.8, preferred-class form.**  Under Stacks 09SR a
`t`-structure in the preferred class is boundedly equivalent to the
`t`-structure compactly generated by any compact zero-detecting object. -/
theorem tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass
    [HasCoproducts.{v} C] (h09 : Tag09SRPaper C)
    {t tH : TStructure C} (ht : InPreferredClass t) {H : C}
    (hHc : IsCompactAb H) (hHg : IsPaperGenerator H)
    (hgenH : tH.le 0 = Coprod (shiftTail H 0)) : TStructureEquivalent t tH := by
  obtain ⟨G, tG, hGc, hGg, hgenG, hteq⟩ := ht
  exact tStructureEquivalent_trans hteq
    (tStructureEquivalent_of_isClassicalGeneratorOnCompacts tG tH G H hgenG hgenH
      (h09 inferInstance G hGc hGg) (h09 inferInstance H hHc hHg) hGc hHc)

/-- Approximation data at a preferred `t`-structure can be moved to any
compactly generated `t`-structure with any compact zero-detecting generator:
generator change followed by `t`-structure change. -/
theorem exists_paperData_at_generated
    [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated C] [HasCoproducts.{v} C] (h09 : Tag09SRPaper C)
    (W : PaperWeakApproximationData C) (hpref : InPreferredClass W.t)
    {H : C} (tH : TStructure C)
    (hHc : IsCompactAb H) (hHg : IsPaperGenerator H)
    (hgenH : tH.le 0 = Coprod (shiftTail H 0)) :
    ∃ W' : PaperWeakApproximationData C, W'.G = H ∧ W'.t = tH := by
  obtain ⟨W₁, hG₁, ht₁⟩ := exists_changeGenerator_of_tag09SR h09 W hHc hHg
  have heq : TStructureEquivalent W₁.t tH := by
    rw [ht₁]
    exact tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass h09 hpref hHc hHg hgenH
  exact ⟨SchemeOpenClosedGlueM3Smww27cuj.rebasePaperWeakApproximationDataTStructure
    W₁ tH heq, hG₁, rfl⟩

end Abstract

/-! ### Recollement frames without approximation packages -/

section Frame

variable {DZ : Type uZ} {DX : Type uD} {DU : Type uU}
  [Category.{v} DZ] [Category.{v} DX] [Category.{v} DU]
  [Preadditive DZ] [Preadditive DX] [Preadditive DU]
  [HasZeroObject DZ] [HasZeroObject DX] [HasZeroObject DU]
  [HasShift DZ ℤ] [HasShift DX ℤ] [HasShift DU ℤ]
  [∀ (n : ℤ), (shiftFunctor DZ n).Additive]
  [∀ (n : ℤ), (shiftFunctor DX n).Additive]
  [∀ (n : ℤ), (shiftFunctor DU n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated DZ] [Pretriangulated DX] [Pretriangulated DU]
  [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated DZ] [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated DX]
  [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated DU]

variable (DZ DX DU) in
/-- **LP26 Lemma 4.3 (`lem:normalize`) / Setup 4.4 (`setup:standing`) data
without approximation packages.**  This is `PaperOpenEndpointSetup` with the
open approximation package `approxU` replaced by compactness and zero
detection of the open generator `G_U`.  No field mentions weak
approximability of any of the three categories. -/
structure OpenClosedFrame where
  /-- The recollement `D_Z → D → D_U`. -/
  R : Recollement DZ DX DU
  /-- The middle `t`-structure, compactly generated by the normalized generator. -/
  tD : TStructure DX
  /-- The closed `t`-structure, compactly generated by `i^*` of it. -/
  tZ : TStructure DZ
  /-- The open `t`-structure, compactly generated by `G_U`. -/
  tU : TStructure DU
  /-- The open generator. -/
  GU : DU
  GU_compact : IsCompactAb GU
  GU_paperGenerates : IsPaperGenerator GU
  /-- A compact generator of the middle category (LP26 Lemma 4.3). -/
  G' : DX
  G'_compact : IsCompactAb G'
  G'_paperGenerates : IsPaperGenerator G'
  /-- The normalizing shift of LP26 Lemma 4.3(1). -/
  m : ℤ
  jStar_G'_mem : tU.le m (R.jStar.obj G')
  [normalized_biproduct : HasBinaryBiproduct (G'⟦m⟧) (R.jShriek.obj GU)]
  tD_compactlyGenerated :
    tD.le 0 = Coprod (shiftTail (G'⟦m⟧ ⊞ R.jShriek.obj GU) 0)
  tZ_compactlyGenerated :
    tZ.le 0 = Coprod (shiftTail (R.iStar.obj (G'⟦m⟧ ⊞ R.jShriek.obj GU)) 0)
  tU_compactlyGenerated : tU.le 0 = Coprod (shiftTail GU 0)

attribute [instance] OpenClosedFrame.normalized_biproduct

namespace OpenClosedFrame

variable (F : OpenClosedFrame DZ DX DU)

include F

/-- The normalized middle generator `G'[m] ⊕ j_!G_U`. -/
abbrev normalizedGenerator : DX := F.G'⟦F.m⟧ ⊞ F.R.jShriek.obj F.GU

theorem normalizedGenerator_compact : IsCompactAb F.normalizedGenerator :=
  isCompactAb_normalizedGenerator F.R F.G' F.GU F.m F.G'_compact F.GU_compact

theorem normalizedGenerator_paperGenerates : IsPaperGenerator F.normalizedGenerator :=
  (lemma_4_3_2_paperGeneration F.R F.G' F.GU F.m F.G'_paperGenerates).1

/-- `i^*` of the normalized generator is compact: `i^*` is left adjoint to
`i_*`, which preserves coproducts because it is itself a left adjoint
(`i_* ⊣ i^!`). -/
theorem closedGenerator_compact : IsCompactAb (F.R.iStar.obj F.normalizedGenerator) :=
  isCompactAb_leftAdjoint_obj' F.R.iStarAdj F.normalizedGenerator_compact
    (fun _ => F.R.iLowerAdj.leftAdjoint_preservesColimits.preservesColimitsOfShape)

theorem closedGenerator_paperGenerates :
    IsPaperGenerator (F.R.iStar.obj F.normalizedGenerator) :=
  (lemma_4_3_2_paperGeneration F.R F.G' F.GU F.m F.G'_paperGenerates).2

/-- Complete a frame with an open approximation package matched exactly. -/
def toPaperOpenEndpointSetup (WU : PaperWeakApproximationData DU)
    (ht : WU.t = F.tU) (hG : WU.G = F.GU) :
    SchemeTwoOpenM3.PaperOpenEndpointSetup DZ DX DU where
  R := F.R
  tD := F.tD
  tZ := F.tZ
  tU := F.tU
  approxU := WU
  GU := F.GU
  G' := F.G'
  G'_compact := F.G'_compact
  G'_paperGenerates := F.G'_paperGenerates
  m := F.m
  jStar_G'_mem := F.jStar_G'_mem
  tD_compactlyGenerated := F.tD_compactlyGenerated
  tZ_compactlyGenerated := F.tZ_compactlyGenerated
  tU_compactlyGenerated := F.tU_compactlyGenerated
  approxU_t := ht
  approxU_G := hG

/-- **LP26 Theorem 1.1 at arbitrary endpoint packages.**  Given a frame,
approximation data on the two ends at any `t`-structures in Neeman's preferred
class (with arbitrary generators), Stacks 09SR on the three categories, and
positive Hom vanishing between compacts of the middle, the middle category
admits approximation data at **any** preferred `t`-structure `sD`. -/
theorem exists_paperData
    [HasCoproducts.{v} DZ] [HasCoproducts.{v} DX] [HasCoproducts.{v} DU]
    (h09Z : Tag09SRPaper DZ) (h09X : Tag09SRPaper DX) (h09U : Tag09SRPaper DU)
    (WZ : PaperWeakApproximationData DZ) (hZ : InPreferredClass WZ.t)
    (WU : PaperWeakApproximationData DU) (hU : InPreferredClass WU.t)
    (hvan : CompactHomZeroAtTop DX)
    (sD : TStructure DX) (hD : InPreferredClass sD) :
    ∃ W : PaperWeakApproximationData DX, W.t = sD := by
  obtain ⟨WZ', hGZ, htZ⟩ := exists_paperData_at_generated h09Z WZ hZ F.tZ
    F.closedGenerator_compact F.closedGenerator_paperGenerates F.tZ_compactlyGenerated
  obtain ⟨WU', hGU, htU⟩ := exists_paperData_at_generated h09U WU hU F.tU
    F.GU_compact F.GU_paperGenerates F.tU_compactlyGenerated
  let M := (F.toPaperOpenEndpointSetup WU' htU hGU).toPaperSetupMainMinimal
    (DZ := DZ) (DX := DX) (DU := DU) WZ' htZ hGZ
  obtain ⟨W, ht, _⟩ :=
    SchemeTwoOpenM3.PaperSetupMainMinimal.exists_paperData_of_compactHomZeroAtTop M hvan
  have heq : TStructureEquivalent W.t sD := by
    apply tStructureEquivalent_symm
    rw [ht]
    exact tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass h09X hD
      F.normalizedGenerator_compact F.normalizedGenerator_paperGenerates
      F.tD_compactlyGenerated
  exact ⟨SchemeOpenClosedGlueM3Smww27cuj.rebasePaperWeakApproximationDataTStructure
    W sD heq, rfl⟩

/-- A frame is no stronger than the repository's existing open-endpoint
setup: forgetting `approxU` (and keeping the compactness and zero detection of
its generator) gives a frame with the same recollement, `t`-structures and
generators. -/
def ofPaperOpenEndpointSetup (S : SchemeTwoOpenM3.PaperOpenEndpointSetup DZ DX DU) :
    OpenClosedFrame DZ DX DU where
  R := S.R
  tD := S.tD
  tZ := S.tZ
  tU := S.tU
  GU := S.GU
  GU_compact := S.approxU_G ▸ S.approxU.G_compact
  GU_paperGenerates := S.approxU_G ▸ S.approxU.G_paperGenerates
  G' := S.G'
  G'_compact := S.G'_compact
  G'_paperGenerates := S.G'_paperGenerates
  m := S.m
  jStar_G'_mem := S.jStar_G'_mem
  normalized_biproduct := S.normalized_biproduct
  tD_compactlyGenerated := S.tD_compactlyGenerated
  tZ_compactlyGenerated := S.tZ_compactlyGenerated
  tU_compactlyGenerated := S.tU_compactlyGenerated

end OpenClosedFrame

end Frame

/-! ### The scheme-level open/closed step -/

section SupportedScheme

open AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
open RelativeFM.SchemeWeakApproxStatementM1
open RelativeFM.SchemeNeemanFiniteCoverAssemblyM5
open RelativeFM.SchemeOpenClosedGlueM3Smww27cuj

/-- Per-category inputs on the repository's `D_qc,Z(X)` model, for `X` qcqs and
`Z` closed with quasi-compact complement.  Each field is a statement about one
category, independent of any recollement or approximation package. -/
structure SupportedCategoryInput : Prop where
  /-- Small coproducts in `D_qc,Z(X)` (the existing completion's
  `coproduct*` fields). -/
  coproducts : ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Z : Closeds X), IsCompactClosedComplement Z →
      HasCoproducts.{u + 1} (DqcSupported X Z)
  /-- Stacks Tag **09SR** in `D_qc,Z(X)` (AxiomMath/Stacks
  `isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_iff_triangEnvelope_eq_isCompactObject_and_isCompactlyGenerated`). -/
  tag_09SR : ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Z : Closeds X), IsCompactClosedComplement Z → Tag09SRPaper (DqcSupported X Z)
  /-- Neeman 2024, Theorem **3.2(iii)**: the restricted standard `t`-structure is
  in the preferred equivalence class. -/
  neeman_3_2_iii : ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Z : Closeds X), IsCompactClosedComplement Z →
      InPreferredClass (dqcSupportedStandardTStructure X Z)
  /-- Positive Hom vanishing between compacts of `D_qc,Z(X)` (the existing
  completion's `compactHomZeroAtTop`; Stacks 09MB with 0AED). -/
  compactHomZeroAtTop : ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Z : Closeds X), IsCompactClosedComplement Z → CompactHomZeroAtTop (DqcSupported X Z)

/-- The recollement frame for each qcqs open/closed situation: GL26 Appendix A
open/closed localization of `D_qc,Z(X)` with LP26 Lemma 4.3 normalization data
and compactly generated `t`-structures.  No approximation package occurs. -/
def OpenClosedFrameInput : Prop :=
  ∀ {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] (V : X.Opens)
    (Z : Closeds X), IsCompactClosedComplement Z → IsCompactOpen V →
    Nonempty (OpenClosedFrame (DqcSupported X (closedDiff V Z)) (DqcSupported X Z)
      (DqcSupported V (openClosedSupport V Z)))

/-- **The compact open/closed field of the qcqs induction**, from a frame and the
per-category inputs.  Unlike the deleted `compact_open_closed_glue_of_completionInput`, the
geometric input does not depend on the two endpoint packages. -/
theorem compact_open_closed_glue_of_frameInput
    (K : SupportedCategoryInput.{u}) (J : OpenClosedFrameInput.{u}) :
    ∀ {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
      (V : X.Opens) (Z : Closeds X),
      IsCompactClosedComplement Z → IsCompactOpen V →
      NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability X (closedDiff V Z) →
      NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability V (openClosedSupport V Z) →
      NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability X Z := by
  intro X _ _ V Z hcZ hcV hclosed hopen
  obtain ⟨⟨WZ, hWZ⟩⟩ := hclosed
  obtain ⟨⟨WU, hWU⟩⟩ := hopen
  obtain ⟨F⟩ := J V Z hcZ hcV
  have hcZ₁ : IsCompactClosedComplement (closedDiff V Z) := by
    change _root_.IsCompact ((Z : Set X) \ (V : Set X))ᶜ
    rw [Set.compl_sdiff]
    exact hcV.union hcZ
  have : CompactSpace V := isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp hcV
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace V :=
    QuasiSeparatedSpace.of_isOpenEmbedding V.ι.isOpenEmbedding
  have hcZU : IsCompactClosedComplement (openClosedSupport V Z) :=
    SchemeSupportedFiniteCoverInductionM5.isCompact_compl_openSupport V (Z : Set X)
      hcV Z.isClosed hcZ
  have := K.coproducts X (closedDiff V Z) hcZ₁
  have := K.coproducts X Z hcZ
  have := K.coproducts V (openClosedSupport V Z) hcZU
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := F.exists_paperData
    (K.tag_09SR X _ hcZ₁) (K.tag_09SR X Z hcZ) (K.tag_09SR V _ hcZU)
    WZ (hWZ ▸ K.neeman_3_2_iii X _ hcZ₁)
    WU (hWU ▸ K.neeman_3_2_iii V _ hcZU)
    (K.compactHomZeroAtTop X Z hcZ)
    (dqcSupportedStandardTStructure X Z) (K.neeman_3_2_iii X Z hcZ)
  exact ⟨⟨W, hW⟩⟩

/-- **Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2(iv), qcqs supported form**, with the open/closed
step supplied by a frame.  For `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated and `Z ⊆ X`
closed with quasi-compact complement, `D_qc,Z(X)` with its restricted standard
`t`-structure is weakly approximable (`NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability X Z`).

Inputs: the affine supported base `of_isAffine`; Stacks 08DF (supported
excision); the per-category inputs `K` (coproducts, Stacks 09SR, Neeman
3.2(iii), compact Hom vanishing); and the frame input `J`.  Isomorphism transport
is proved (`SchemeNeemanIsoTransportM4.neemanSupportedWeakApproximability_of_iso`). -/
theorem neemanSupported_of_qcqs_of_frameInput
    (of_isAffine : ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsAffine X] (Z : Closeds X),
      IsCompactClosedComplement Z → NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability X Z)
    (S : SchemeSupportedExcisionM2.StacksSupportedExcisionInput.{u})
    (K : SupportedCategoryInput.{u}) (J : OpenClosedFrameInput.{u})
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Z : Closeds X) (hcZ : IsCompactClosedComplement Z) :
    NeemanSupportedWeakApproximability X Z :=
  neemanSupported_of_qcqs_with_compactGlue
    { of_isAffine := of_isAffine
      of_iso := fun e Z h =>
        SchemeNeemanIsoTransportM4.neemanSupportedWeakApproximability_of_iso e Z h
      excision := fun U Z hsub h =>
        SchemeSupportedExcisionM2.neemanSupportedWeakApproximability_of_stacksExcision S U Z hsub h
      open_closed_glue := compact_open_closed_glue_of_frameInput K J }
    X Z hcZ

end SupportedScheme

/-! ### Non-vacuity of the abstract generator change -/

section NonVacuity

/-- The hypotheses of `exists_changeGenerator` are satisfiable: in the small-Hom
affine derived category `D(A)` (which has small coproducts) the proved
regular-module data can be changed to its own generator. -/
example (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    let H := Spaltenstein.affineSpaltensteinInput A
    ∃ W' : PaperWeakApproximationData (SmallAffineD A H),
      W'.G = (AffineNeemanEndpointM3.smallRegularModulePaperData A H).G ∧
        W'.t = (AffineNeemanEndpointM3.smallRegularModulePaperData A H).t := by
  intro H
  have : HasCoproducts.{u} (SmallAffineD A H) := smallAffineHasCoproductsOfUnivLE A H
  let W := AffineNeemanEndpointM3.smallRegularModulePaperData A H
  exact exists_changeGenerator W W.G_compact W.G_paperGenerates
    (ObjectProperty.le_triangEnvelope _ _ ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff _ _).mpr rfl))
    (ObjectProperty.le_triangEnvelope _ _ ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff _ _).mpr rfl))

end NonVacuity

